## Original Content
Dans sa décision, le juge Paul Engelmayer a estimé que les arguments soulevés par la fille de Robert Maxwell, selon lesquels ses droits constitutionnels avaient été bafoués, étaient dénués de fondements sérieux.

## Summary
Judge Paul Engelmayer rejected Ghislaine Maxwell's appeal to cancel her conviction, dismissing her claims of constitutional rights violations as lacking serious foundation. This decision is part of the legal proceedings related to the Epstein affair.

## Key Points
- Ghislaine Maxwell's appeal to overturn her conviction was rejected by Judge Paul Engelmayer.
- Her arguments regarding constitutional rights violations were deemed without serious grounds.
- The ruling pertains to the Epstein case and its legal repercussions.


